<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajadhiraja Chola</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1054</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Rajadhiraja I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rajadhiraja <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> was a Chola king, the eldest son of Rajendra I, who was co-ruler from 1018 and sole ruler from 1044 to 1054. A warlike king, he campaigned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> and repeatedly against the Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukyas</a>, and claimed to have sacked their capital Kalyani. He was killed in 1054 at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-koppam">Battle of Koppam</a> while fighting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/someshvara-i">Someshvara I</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rajadhiraja-chola.jpg" alt="Rajadhiraja Chola" width="320" height="165" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Rajadhiraja_Chola.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
